# Hand-written sample in the SUBSET-076 format family, for
# evc_s076_check development (test/src/evc_s076_check.adb): a valid
# balise telegram (packet 0, the Virtual Balise Cover marker) and a
# valid radio message (message 5), both built with our own encoder so
# that the "var" rows below are exactly what SUBSET-076's own reference
# decoder would emit. Kept until the sibling checkout has real ones.
sequence VBC and message 5
meta author: evc_s076_check development
case packet 0 on a short telegram
step balise group read
text: a balise sends a telegram with packet 0 and no other information
telegram 1 1 1/1 0 bits 210 a000028020008003ffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffffc0
var Q_UPDOWN 1 1
var M_VERSION 7 32
var Q_MEDIA 1 0
var N_PIG 3 0
var N_TOTAL 3 0
var M_DUP 2 0
var M_MCOUNT 8 5
var NID_C 10 1
var NID_BG 14 1
var Q_LINK 1 0
var NID_PACKET 8 0
var NID_VBCMK 6 3 ; virtual balise cover marker
var NID_PACKET 8 255
result: accepted
case message 5, track to train
step radio message received
text: an RBC sends message 5 (MA without packets)
message 1 0 nid 5 bits 112 050380000c0e4008004000060720
var NID_MESSAGE 8 5
var L_MESSAGE 10 14
var T_TRAIN 32 12345
var M_ACK 1 0
var NID_C 10 1
var NID_BG 14 2
var T_TRAIN 32 12345
result: accepted
